#: patterns/faq.php:14
msgid "Do I need to know how to code?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:14
msgid "No. Pages, templates, headers, footers, colors and fonts are all edited visually in the Site Editor. Code is there if you want it, never required."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:15
msgid "Will it work with my plugins?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:15
msgid "Praxis uses standard WordPress blocks and templates, so plugins that support block themes work as expected, including forms, SEO and e-commerce."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:16
msgid "Can I change the colors and fonts?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:16
msgid "Yes. Pick one of the style variations or set your own colors and fonts in Appearance → Editor → Styles. Every page updates at once."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:17
msgid "Is it accessible?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:17
msgid "The default palette is checked for WCAG AA contrast, focus styles are always visible, and animations switch off for people who prefer reduced motion."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:18
msgid "How do I customise it safely?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:18
msgid "Use the included Praxis Child theme for code changes, so updates to Praxis never overwrite your work. Changes made in the Site Editor are kept automatically."
msgstr ""

